{"name":"Still Moment","hex":"#cbc4b2","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"still","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Not moving; calm.","Not effervescing; not sparkling."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Without motion.","Up to a time, as in the preceding time."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/still"},{"term":"moment","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A particular point, or relatively small region.\nA particular point of space; a spot.","A particular point of space; a spot."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moment"}],"entries":[{"title":"Still","blocks":[{"text":"A still is an apparatus used to distill liquid mixtures by heating to selectively boil and then cooling to condense the vapor. A still uses the same concepts as a basic distillation apparatus, but on a much larger scale. Stills have been used to produce perfume and medicine, water for injection (WFI) for pharmaceutical use, generally to separate and purify different chemicals, and to produce distilled beverages containing ethanol."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Glenfiddich_Distillery_stills.jpg/330px-Glenfiddich_Distillery_stills.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Still","wikidata":"Q1436130"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/A_still_at_Mackmyra_Whisky_Distillery.jpg/500px-A_still_at_Mackmyra_Whisky_Distillery.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/A_still_at_Mackmyra_Whisky_Distillery.jpg/1280px-A_still_at_Mackmyra_Whisky_Distillery.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/A_still_at_Mackmyra_Whisky_Distillery.jpg/500px-A_still_at_Mackmyra_Whisky_Distillery.jpg?utm_source=